From 78932b6060790ef2a7a9c891905f6e397472565e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:17:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Doxygen: no warning, comments checked against the code

Doxygen 1.9.8, run as the doxygen job of the continuous integration, gave
821 warnings on gpu-proto (0 upstream); it now gives none:

- the parameters of the declarations documented with \param are named
  (names of the definitions); no other change of the code;
- the 37 undocumented overloads (CRTP standard and FBar integrators,
  Faltus2026, matrix-free operators, FixedPoint, AmgX) are documented;
- PREDEFINED contains MFEM_USE_CUDSS and MFEM_MGIS_HAVE_AMGX, so that the
  cuDSS and AmgX solvers appear in the documentation.

The comments of the files changed by the prototype were also checked
against the code (157 fixes): layout of the element matrices with vdim
(heat transfer, micromorphic damage), priority of the post-processings
computation with --execution, shallPrint, Steffensen acceleration on the
host, names of the parameters (use_device, communicator of AmgXSolver),
kernels compiled as CUDA or HIP code, getMPISize, execution settings and
memory of MFEM in Material and MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator. The
\author lines of the six micromorphic files, removed by a previous commit,
are restored.
